{"name":"Taiwan Gold","hex":"#c7aa71","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gold","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heavy yellow elemental metal of great value, with atomic number 79.","A coin or coinage made of this material, or supposedly so."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["☉ (alchemy)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gold"}],"entries":[{"title":"Taiwan","blocks":[{"text":"Taiwan, officially the Republic of China (ROC), is a country in East Asia. The main island of Taiwan, formerly known as Formosa, lies between the East and South China Seas in the northwestern Pacific Ocean, with the People's Republic of China (PRC) to the northwest, Japan to the northeast, and the Philippines to the south. It has an area of 35,808 square kilometers, with mountain ranges dominating the eastern two-thirds and plains in the western third, where its highly urbanized population is concentrated. The combined territories under ROC control consist of 168 islands in total covering 36,193 square kilometers. The largest metropolitan area is formed by Taipei, New Taipei City, and Keelung. With around 23.9 million inhabitants, Taiwan is among the most densely populated countries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Flag_of_the_Republic_of_China.svg/330px-Flag_of_the_Republic_of_China.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiwan","wikidata":"Q865"},{"title":"Gold","blocks":[{"text":"Gold is a chemical element; its chemical symbol is Au and atomic number 79. In its pure form, it is a bright-metallic-yellow, dense, soft, malleable, and ductile metal. Chemically, gold is a transition metal, a group 11 element, and one of the noble metals. It is one of the least reactive chemical elements, being the second lowest in the reactivity series, with only platinum ranked as less reactive. Gold is solid under standard conditions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Gold-crystals.jpg/330px-Gold-crystals.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold","wikidata":"Q897"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/%E5%8D%91%E5%8D%97%E9%81%BA%E5%9D%80%E4%BA%BA%E7%8D%B8%E5%BD%A2%E7%8E%89%E7%8E%A6.jpg/500px-%E5%8D%91%E5%8D%97%E9%81%BA%E5%9D%80%E4%BA%BA%E7%8D%B8%E5%BD%A2%E7%8E%89%E7%8E%A6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/%E5%8D%91%E5%8D%97%E9%81%BA%E5%9D%80%E4%BA%BA%E7%8D%B8%E5%BD%A2%E7%8E%89%E7%8E%A6.jpg/500px-%E5%8D%91%E5%8D%97%E9%81%BA%E5%9D%80%E4%BA%BA%E7%8D%B8%E5%BD%A2%E7%8E%89%E7%8E%A6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"2,300-year-old jade, unearthed at Beinan Cultural Park","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%E5%8D%91%E5%8D%97%E9%81%BA%E5%9D%80%E4%BA%BA%E7%8D%B8%E5%BD%A2%E7%8E%89%E7%8E%A6.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Tainan_Taiwan_Fort-Zeelandia-01.jpg/500px-Tainan_Taiwan_Fort-Zeelandia-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Tainan_Taiwan_Fort-Zeelandia-01.jpg/1280px-Tainan_Taiwan_Fort-Zeelandia-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Tainan_Taiwan_Fort-Zeelandia-01.jpg/500px-Tainan_Taiwan_F